WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.340
Three equations.

2
00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:02.610
Three unknowns.

3
00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:04.250
Surely that's enough?

4
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:07.240
Picture each equation as a sheet of card.

5
00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:10.840
Push three together, and they
can meet at a single point.

6
00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:14.700
Tilt them, and they share a
line, like the pages of a book.

7
00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:17.340
Now slide them into a new arrangement.

8
00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:20.260
Is there still somewhere all three meet?

9
00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:25.500
So how can three equations in three
unknowns have no solution at all?

10
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:29.890
In this mission, you'll see each
equation in three unknowns as a plane,

11
00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:33.150
and a unique solution as one common point.

12
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:37.850
You'll solve by elimination: use one
equation to remove a variable from the other

13
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:38.890
two.

14
00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:44.510
Your mission: explain how three equations
in three unknowns can have no solution.
